  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37130472",
      "title": "Importing Features From Packages",
      "lectureOrder": 18,
      "videoOrder": 17,
      "sourceHash": "92ee731ea5813ba5885ec0c4420361c40b6af453dcc6450b153530f2e5a240fb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 3.18,
          "en": "So the code editor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.18,
          "end": 5.28,
          "en": "doesn't find the runApp function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.28,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "It doesn't know where runApp comes from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.22,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "Now of course, I showed you that runApp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 12.75,
          "en": "is defined in the Flutter framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.75,
          "end": 14.4,
          "en": "It's coming from Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.4,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "but when writing code, you have to be very explicit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "You have to tell your program",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 21.15,
          "en": "that runApp is coming from Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.15,
          "end": 23.88,
          "en": "It's not guessing that this could be the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 26.37,
          "en": "There are hundreds and thousands of libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.37,
          "end": 28.41,
          "en": "and packages out there in the world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 28.41,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "written by other developers, and therefore, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 33.66,
          "en": "your code and your code editor doesn't guess",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 33.66,
          "end": 37.08,
          "en": "from which of these many packages this runApp function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 38.163,
          "en": "might be coming from.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.27,
          "end": 41.7,
          "en": "Instead, you have to tell your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.7,
          "end": 44.73,
          "en": "And for that, the first important step in a Dart program",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.73,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "is to go to the pubspec.yaml file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "because in that file, you can manage the dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "the third-party dependencies of your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 54.84,
          "en": "You can reference other libraries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.84,
          "end": 57.39,
          "en": "or frameworks from which you want to use code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57.39,
          "end": 58.92,
          "en": "in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 58.92,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "And in there, under dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 63.72,
          "en": "you have to add all third-party packages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.72,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "which you want to use as dependencies in your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 68.403,
          "en": "so from which you want to use features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 72.87,
          "en": "Now here, Flutter is actually already added as a dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 72.87,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "so we don't need to change anything there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 76.26,
          "en": "but it is important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "that this entry must exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 81.21000000000001,
          "en": "in order to use features from that package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 82.86,
          "en": "Of course, here we're still getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 82.86,
          "end": 86.19,
          "en": "despite having added this package in the pubspec.yaml file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 86.19,
          "end": 87.84,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 87.84,
          "end": 89.61,
          "en": "even though we added this dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 89.61,
          "end": 92.94,
          "en": "our code still doesn't magically look into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "those dependencies which we added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "and then check if there is some runApp function anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "in that third-party code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 102.69,
          "en": "Instead, we have to add a so-called import statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 102.69,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "at the top of the file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 106.83,
          "en": "And we do this by using a special keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 106.83,
          "end": 110.25,
          "en": "the import keyword, which is built into Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 110.25,
          "end": 112.74000000000001,
          "en": "The import keyword tells Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 112.74000000000001,
          "end": 116.07,
          "en": "that we wanna kind of connect our code file here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 116.07,
          "end": 119.94,
          "en": "our main.dart code file here, with another code file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 119.94,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "or to be more precise that we want to use certain features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "certain functions, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 127.98,
          "en": "that are defined in some other code file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 127.98,
          "end": 130.23,
          "en": "in this code file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "And for that, we have to add a so-called import path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 134.88,
          "en": "after the import keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 134.88,
          "end": 139.05,
          "en": "where we specify from which file we wanna import something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 139.05,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "You define such a path by adding opening and closing quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "double quotes or single quotes, that is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 149.7,
          "en": "but single quotes are more common in Dart projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "And then since we want to import some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 153.15,
          "en": "from a package here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 153.15,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "we start by writing package followed by a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 159.213,
          "en": "and then followed by the package name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 162.87,
          "en": "Now you see I'm getting some auto suggestions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 162.87,
          "end": 165.72,
          "en": "by my code editor, which is a very useful feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 165.72,
          "end": 167.64,
          "en": "because it can speed up development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 167.64,
          "end": 171.99,
          "en": "and it also reduces the danger of introducing typos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 173.76,
          "en": "since we can use these suggestions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 173.76,
          "end": 177.6,
          "en": "to auto complete our code, as I'll show you in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 178.56,
          "en": "But here at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 178.56,
          "end": 180.6,
          "en": "I don't have any suggestion that I need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "Instead, I need some functionality from the Flutter package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 186.66,
          "en": "Hence, after the colon, we type Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 186.66,
          "end": 189.22,
          "en": "and you see that my suggestions are changing now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 190.17,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "and then we want to get access to some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "that's defined in some specific file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 195.69,
          "en": "in that Flutter package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 195.69,
          "end": 198.81,
          "en": "And hence we create a path to that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "by adding a forward slash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 204.15,
          "en": "And then for us, it's the material.dart file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 204.15,
          "end": 205.863,
          "en": "from which we want to get code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 206.7,
          "end": 208.35,
          "en": "If I type MA here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 208.35,
          "end": 211.53,
          "en": "the suggestions are narrowed down even more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 211.53,
          "end": 212.94,
          "en": "And now as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 212.94,
          "end": 215.7,
          "en": "it's this material.dart file I'm interested in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 215.7,
          "end": 218.16,
          "en": "so we can select this with the arrow keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 218.16,
          "end": 221.97,
          "en": "and hit tab to auto complete this path here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 221.97,
          "end": 224.28,
          "en": "And that's the part that can speed up development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 224.28,
          "end": 225.903,
          "en": "and also avoid typos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 226.8,
          "end": 228.96,
          "en": "Now we must end this with a semicolon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 228.96,
          "end": 232.45,
          "en": "because basically all your statements must end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 232.45,
          "end": 234.24,
          "en": "with a semicolon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 234.24,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "Function definitions are an exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 239.25,
          "en": "You don't add semicolons here after the opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 241.135,
          "en": "or closing curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 241.135,
          "end": 244.23,
          "en": "but Visual Studio Code also tells us that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 244.23,
          "end": 246.75,
          "en": "this semicolon here is unexpected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 246.75,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "so you can't really get this wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 252.27,
          "en": "It also tells you if you forget a semicolon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 252.27,
          "end": 253.98,
          "en": "Here, if I scroll down,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 253.98,
          "end": 256.74,
          "en": "the error messages are always at the bottom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 256.74,
          "end": 260.133,
          "en": "I also get an error that a semicolon would've been expected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 261,
          "end": 263.91,
          "en": "And with that, we have a valid import statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 263.91,
          "end": 266.91,
          "en": "And now the runApp error went away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 266.91,
          "end": 268.77,
          "en": "And you also might have noticed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 268.77,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "that the color changed from white,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 272.55,
          "en": "which is always a good indicator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 272.55,
          "end": 276.633,
          "en": "that some identifier wasn't found to a light yellow color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 279.12,
          "en": "I still have an error here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 279.12,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "but that's now a different error, which we'll tackle next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 283.89,
          "en": "But now runApp is found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 283.89,
          "end": 287.49,
          "en": "because material.dart in the end gives us access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 287.49,
          "end": 291.63,
          "en": "to the runApp function to find by Flutter in their code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 291.63,
          "end": 293.90999999999997,
          "en": "And that of course was a lot of talking about this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 293.90999999999997,
          "end": 295.71,
          "en": "but understanding functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 295.71,
          "end": 297.96,
          "en": "calling functions and function definitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 297.96,
          "end": 301.443,
          "en": "and how Flutter apps start is of course very important.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
